INT. BIRTHDAY PARTY BACKYARD - DAY

Balloons. Folding tables. A bouncy castle deflating in the corner. Forty children, screaming.

WALDO PIMM (40s, sequined vest, top hat, rabbit in a cage) stands on a milk crate, juggling three oranges. One slips. He catches it with his chin.

WALDO
(to the kids)
Ladies and gentlemen! The Great Waldo!

A child screams. Another cries. A third throws cake.

WALDO (CONT'D)
(muttering)
Sixty dollars. Sixty dollars. Sixty dollars.

He pulls a scarf from his sleeve. It keeps coming. Yards of it. He tugs. Tugs. Out comes a second scarf, then a third, tied together, and finally a live parakeet that flies straight over the fence.

WALDO (CONT'D)
(to the sky)
That was Gerald.

A woman's voice calls from the gate.

BERNICE PLUMMER-ASANTE (70s, sunhat, enormous handbag) pushes through, waving a rolled newspaper at Waldo, who ducks. The rabbit escapes its cage, hops across the lawn, and disappears under the cake table. Bernice swings and misses. Waldo vaults the crate, a child grabs his cape, and the three of them end up in a heap beside the bouncy castle, the castle sighing down on top of them.

BERNICE
You owe me for the parakeet!

WALDO
(muffled)
He's a free spirit!
